; E = sum over joints of tau_i * |delta-theta_i|
; the total work done moving along a trajectory regardless of speed
; speed-invariant: svabhava of the path, not of the motion plan
; P = E / T: power decreases as T grows; T* = sqrt(E) balances T and P
; sangati roots: gati (the path whose energy this measures), krama (ordered
; sum over joints), svabhava (intrinsic to the path — invariant to speed)

(kosha path-energy
  (vishesa mechanical-energy-varga)
  (swarupa gati)
  (sthita krama trajectory)
  (siddha svabhava)
  (yukta torque angular-displacement)
  (abheda energy work)
  (janaka velocity-plan)
  (apeksha power))
